{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Fix pushed for review — Gerrit change 2333\n\nhttps://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/2333 (commit `8d72cbf414f4`, branch\n`reb-71fe-wellknown-edge-route`). NOT submitted, NOT deployed; nginx on the box was not\nreloaded.\n\n### The change\n\n`infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template` — one new exact-match location in the port-443 server\nblock, immediately before `location /`:\n\n    location = /.well-known/oauth-protected-resource/mcp {\n        proxy_pass http://rebar_mcp;\n        ...forwarded headers + the same proxy_redirect http->https rules as the /mcp blocks\n        proxy_http_version 1.1;\n        proxy_set_header Connection \"\";\n    }\n\nNo URI path on `proxy_pass`, so the advertised URI reaches the app verbatim at the path it\nalready answers with 200. It names the `rebar_mcp` upstream rather than a port, so the\nblue-green flip re-points it atomically. Exact match rather than a prefix, so it covers this\none document and cannot widen or reorder anything else under `/.well-known/`.\n\nNothing in the auth path, the 401 challenge text, or `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` was\ntouched.\n\n### Regression tests (`tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py`, +75 lines)\n\nAssert on the RENDERED config, not the raw template: a `_render_nginx()` helper substitutes\nonly `${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}`, and its output was confirmed byte-identical to\n`REVIEW_BOT_PORT=8081 envsubst '${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}' < …`. Hermetic — no gettext binary\nneeded in CI.\n\n- `test_nginx_routes_the_advertised_resource_metadata_url_to_the_mcp_app` — the exact-match\n  location exists and proxies to `http://rebar_mcp` with no URI path.\n- `test_nginx_metadata_route_does_not_shadow_the_acme_challenge` — the rendered config still\n  serves the ACME challenge from `root /var/www/certbot;`.\n- `test_nginx_template_substitutes_cleanly_under_envsubst` — no `${...}` survives rendering.\n\n**Mutation check:** deleting the location block from the template turns\n`test_nginx_routes_the_advertised_resource_metadata_url_to_the_mcp_app` RED (1 failed, 46\npassed); restoring it returns 47 passed.\n\n### Gates\n\n`make lint` clean; `make typecheck` clean (683 files); `pytest\ntests/unit/test_module_size_contract.py` 4 passed; `check_complexity_baseline.py --check`\n`active=39 new=0 increased=0 stale=10`. `tests/unit/test_mcp_on_box_infra.py` 47 passed;\n`tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` + `tests/interfaces/facades/test_mcp_auth.py` 38\npassed.\n\n### Scope note\n\nReiterating the RCA: this is a correctness/standards fix, not the cause of any client-auth\nfailure. Static-bearer clients never fetch `resource_metadata`. Live edge fetchability\nbecomes observable only after the change lands and deploys."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787946861688901655,"uuid":"648868ae-819d-4c82-85e0-6ff691f5fd4d"}